From 863ed0fafb7b41c99eea3e9543aeed6351647915 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: suckbluefrog <suckbluefrog@proton.me>
Date: Tue, 21 Jul 2026 15:24:46 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: wcd939x: route physical headsets through USBSS

The AYN Odin 3 routes its physical 3.5 mm jack through the WCD939x
USBSS switch. Mainline only programs that block for USB, DisplayPort,
and USB-C analog accessory modes, so a detected physical headset is
left without a shared ground and direct left/right paths. This causes
severe channel crossfeed and leaves jack switching dependent on
userspace workarounds.

Add a codec-to-USBSS phandle and an MBHC callback which connects the
physical switch before plug classification and releases it on removal.
Keep DisplayPort AUX ownership when DP is active, then restore a
still-inserted headset when DP disconnects. The USBSS programming mirrors
the vendor HSJ sequence while selecting the codec left/right inputs
directly.

Signed-off-by: suckbluefrog <suckbluefrog@proton.me>
